    (:task
      :id "Task44207"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-442"
      :title "Append-only session trace: every op, gate and mutation with digests"
      :kind :protocol
      :lane "observability"
      :state :planned
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789139870800
      :updatedAt 1789139870800
      :motivation "Measured 2026-09-11: .asl/mem/trace.asn is a twenty-line static matrix that no code writes to, so no stage can answer what actually happened. Reflection had to be reconstructed by re-reading a conversation, and a reverted 1220-line removal was discovered only by chance an hour later. Without an observation log, planning, reflection and verification each rely on the model remembering, which is the failure mode being engineered against."
      :purpose "Every RPC op, gate run and file mutation appends one bounded ASN record to the session trace: timestamp, session, step, op, target, before and after digest, exit status and duration. (:trace [:since N] [:op X] [:limit N]) reads it back. The trace is the shared substrate that plan verify, watch, the gap report and receipts all read; no stage recomputes state from memory."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Append-only trace with digests per mutation" "(:trace …) query with bounds" "Trace is the source for receipts, gap report and watch" "Bounded size with rotation"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "asl/grammar/rpc.asn" ".asl/mem/trace.asn"]
      :targetSymbols ["execute_single_step" "handle_payload"]
      :relatedSymbols ["anchor" "oneStep" "gates"]
      :invariants ["D46" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task44101" "Task44202"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44207"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task44207.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A mutation records both digests and a later external change is visible as a digest mismatch in the trace; a rejected op records the rejection, not a gap." "Reading the trace never rewrites it and respects :limit."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44207" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Verifier fixes an op sequence with known digests." "Implement append with before and after digests." "Implement bounded query." "Rotate on size." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task44208"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-442"
      :title "Coverage and case-diversity map over the corpus"
      :kind :gate
      :lane "observability"
      :state :planned
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789139870800
      :updatedAt 1789139870800
      :motivation "Measured 2026-09-11: no coverage tooling exists in the engine; whether an exported symbol has any test is unknown, and the only quality signal is a substring count of the token (assert. The corpus does contain 1029 negative assertions, so diversity is uneven rather than absent, and nobody can say where. An implementer cannot be asked to raise coverage without a map of what is uncovered."
      :purpose "asl coverage emits an ASN map keyed by package and exported symbol: whether any test references it, which of the twelve case kinds from docs/TEST_CASE_CATALOG.md are detectable in those tests, and once the evaluator resolves imports, whether those tests executed. Kind detection is static and pattern-based, declared as approximate. Gate 7 fails when a package declared covered has symbols with no referencing test."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["asl coverage with per-symbol rows" "Case-kind detection against the catalog" "Executed versus declared once Task43601 lands" "Gate 7 threshold per package"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "docs/TEST_CASE_CATALOG.md"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_gate_7" "collect_tree_files"]
      :relatedSymbols ["gates" "concepts" "bounded"]
      :invariants ["D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task43601" "Task44204"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44208"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task44208.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A symbol with no referencing test is reported uncovered; a suite containing only happy-path cases is reported as one kind; a package whose tests execute zero assertions is reported executed 0 regardless of declared count." "The map is stable across runs and its kind detection is labelled approximate, never presented as proof of quality."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44208" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Verifier fixes packages with known covered and uncovered symbols." "Implement symbol to test reference mapping." "Detect case kinds by pattern." "Join with executed counts." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task44209"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-442"
      :title "Reflection utility: gap report between declared outcomes and observed trace"
      :kind :gate
      :lane "observability"
      :state :planned
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789139870800
      :updatedAt 1789139870800
      :motivation "Measured 2026-09-11: the reflection stage of the epistemic loop had no instrument, so gaps were found by an external reviewer rather than by the system: three duplicated task records, three gates that passed on baseline, amendments silently overwritten and a removal reverted. Self-review by the author is the one mechanism the evidence says degrades results, so reflection must be mechanical."
      :purpose "asl reflect <task> compares the task declared :outcomes and :owns against the session trace and the working tree, and reports: outcomes with no corresponding mutation, mutations outside :owns, files changed by another session since the claim, gates never executed, and receipts whose digest no longer matches. It states findings, never a verdict, and is readable by the grader as evidence."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["asl reflect with ASN findings" "Outcome to mutation correspondence" "Out-of-owns and foreign-change detection" "Stale receipt detection"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c"]
      :targetSymbols ["run_reflect" "execute_single_step"]
      :relatedSymbols ["grading" "anchor" "ssot"]
      :invariants ["D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task44207" "Task44203"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task44209"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task44209.asl"]
